Now I understand the structure. Let me look at the `UA_Array_delete` function again and the `Array_decodeJson_internal` function:

The key issue is in `Array_decodeJson_internal` at line 3130-3131:
```c
/* Save the length of the array */
size_t *p = (size_t*) dst - 1;
*p = length;
```

When `dst` is `&variant->data`, then `(size_t*)dst - 1` points to `variant->arrayLength`. This is how the array length gets set.

Now let me think about the vulnerability. The issue is in `clearStructure`:

```c
ptr += m->padding;
size_t length = *(size_t*)ptr;
ptr += sizeof(size_t);
UA_Array_delete(*(void**)ptr, length, mt);
ptr += sizeof(void*);
```

When clearing a structure that contains a Variant member, `clearStructure` will:
1. Read the `arrayLength` from the Variant struct
2. Read the `data` pointer from the Variant struct
3. Call `UA_Array_delete(data, arrayLength, type)`

But `UA_Array_delete` does:
```c
UA_Array_delete(void *p, size_t size, const UA_DataType *type) {
    if(!type->pointerFree) {
        uintptr_t ptr = (uintptr_t)p;
        for(size_t i = 0; i < size; ++i) {
            UA_clear((void*)ptr, type);
            ptr += type->memSize;
        }
    }
    UA_free((void*)((uintptr_t)p & ~(uintptr_t)UA_EMPTY_ARRAY_SENTINEL));
```

The issue is that `UA_Array_delete` calls `UA_clear` on each element, and `UA_clear` calls `clearJumpTable[type->typeKind](p, type)` followed by `memset(p, 0, type->memSize)`.

But wait, let me look at the `Variant_clear` function again:

```c
Variant_clear(UA_Variant *p, const UA_DataType *_) {
    if(p->storageType != UA_VARIANT_DATA)
        return;
    if(p->type && p->data > UA_EMPTY_ARRAY_SENTINEL) {
        if(p->arrayLength == 0)
            p->arrayLength = 1;
        UA_Array_delete(p->data, p->arrayLength, p->type);
        p->data = NULL;
    }
    if((void*)p->arrayDimensions > UA_EMPTY_ARRAY_SENTINEL)
        UA_free(p->arrayDimensions);
}
```

This looks correct. Let me look at the `clearStructure` function more carefully. The issue might be in how `clearStructure` handles the Variant type.

